Built compress.py using only Python’s standard library, with mixed-radix packing for structured records and a bzip2 fallback for other inputs. Both requested CLI commands work and restore the corpus byte-identically. Compression reduces 44,267 bytes to 16,773 bytes (62.1095%), beating default zlib’s 22,390 bytes. The registered assay checks every restored byte and prints only the reduction percentage; 117 additional round-trip tests also passed.